INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9410','','default','Default values','','7.12'),('9411','','default','Use ISO-8601 week numbers','','none'),('9412','','default','IMPORTANT! If checked, First day of week MUST be set to Monday','','none'),('9413','','default','When using ISO-8601 week numbers, the first day of the week must be set to Monday.','','none'),('9414','','default','Repeats !interval !bymonth !byday !count !until !except. !additional','','none'),('9415','','default','Year','datetime','7.12'),('9416','','default','Month','datetime','7.12'),('9417','','default','Week','datetime','7.10'),('9418','','default','Day','datetime','7.12'),('9419','','default','All Day','','none'),('9420','/dday/admin/modules/list/confirm','default','View Repeating Dates','','7.12'),('9421','/dday/admin/modules/list/confirm','default','Allow user to see a page with all the times a date repeats.','','7.12'),('9422','/dday/admin/modules/list/confirm','default','Administer date tools','','7.12'),('9423','/dday/admin/modules/list/confirm','default','Store a date in the database as a timestamp, deprecated format to support legacy data.','','7.12'),('9424','/dday/admin/modules','default','Configure the Date Popup settings.','','7.12'),('9425','/dday/admin/modules','default','Tools to import and auto-create dates and calendars. ','','7.12'),('9426','/dday/','default','Pop-up calendar','','7.12'),('9427','/dday/admin/config','default','The timezone has been set to !value_link.','','7.12'),('9428','/dday/admin/config','default','The first day of the week has been set to !value_link.','','7.12'),('9429','/dday/admin/config','default','The medium date format has been set to to !value_link.','','7.12'),('9430','/dday/admin/config','default','System date settings','','7.12'),('9431','/dday/admin/config/content/date_popup','default','<p>The Date Popup module allows for manual time entry or use of a jQuery timepicker plugin. The Date module comes with a default jQuery timepicker which is already installed. The module also supports a dropdown timepicker that must be downloaded separately. The dropdown timepicker will not appear as an option until the code is available in the libraries folder. If you do not want to use a jQuery timepicker, you can choose the "Manual time entry" option below and users will get a regular textfield instead.</p>','','7.10');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9432','/dday/admin/config/content/date_popup','default','Use dropdown timepicker','','7.10'),('9433','/dday/admin/config/content/date_popup','default','Manual time entry, no jQuery timepicker','','7.10'),('9434','/dday/admin/config/content/date_popup','default','Timepicker','','7.10'),('9435','/dday/admin/config/content/date_popup','default','<p>To install the dropdown timepicker, create a <code>!directory</code> directory in your site installation. Then visit <a href="@download">@download</a>, download the latest copy and unzip it. You will see files with names like jquery.timepicker-1.1.2.js and jquery.timepicker-1.1.2.css. Rename them to jquery.timepicker.js and jquery.timepicker.css and copy them into <code>!directory</code>.</p>','','7.10'),('9436','/dday/admin/config/content/date_popup','default','<p>The Date Popup calendar includes some css for IE6 that breaks css validation. Since IE 6 is now superceded by IE 7, 8, and 9, the special css for IE 6 has been removed from the regular css used by the Date Popup. If you find you need that css after all, you can add it back in your theme. Look at the way the Garland theme adds special IE-only css in in its page.tpl.php file. The css you need is:</p>','','7.10'),('9437','/dday/admin/help/calendar','default','date_tools','','7.12'),('9438','/dday/node/2/edit','default','Change type','','7.10'),('9439','/dday/node/2/edit','default','Easy creation of date content types and calendars. ','','7.10'),('9440','/dday/admin/people','default','view date repeats','','7.12'),('9441','/dday/admin/people','default','administer date tools','','7.12'),('9442','/dday/admin/structure/types/add','default','Sponsor *test*','','7.12'),('9443','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Imagen sponsor','','7.12'),('9444','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Casillas de selección / botones de opciones','','7.12'),('9445','/dday/node/add','default','Sesión *test*','','7.10'),('9446','/dday/admin/structure/views/add','default','Sesiones','','7.12');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9447','/dday/admin/structure/views/add','default','Sesión','','7.12'),('9448','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/add-item/sessions/page/field','default','Tipo','','7.12'),('9449','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/sessions/page/menu','default','Displays the link in contextual links','','7.12'),('9450','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/edit-details/sessions','default','Optionally, enter a comma delimited list of tags for this view to use in filtering and sorting views on the administrative page.','','7.12'),('9451','/dday/admin/structure/views/view/sessions','default','undo delete of @display_title','','7.12'),('9452','/dday/admin/structure/views/view/sessions/edit/feed','default','Use site default RSS settings','','7.10'),('9453','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/asistentes/block_3/style_plugin','default','Grouping field Nr.@number','','7.12'),('9454','/dday/admin/structure/views/view/asistentes/edit/block_3?destination=node/1','default','Numero de usuarios','','7.12'),('9455','/dday/admin/structure/views/add','default','BOFs','','7.10'),('9456','/dday/admin/structure/views/add','default','Tema del foro','','7.10'),('9457','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session','default','Una <em>conversación de foro</em> comienza una nueva línea de discusión dentro de un foro.','','7.10'),('9458','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Foros','','7.12'),('9459','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Lista de selección','','7.12'),('9460','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Select the date attributes to collect and store.','','7.12'),('9461','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Hour','datetime','7.12');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9462','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Minute','datetime','7.12'),('9463','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Second','datetime','7.12'),('9464','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Date attributes to collect','','7.12'),('9465','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','End dates are used to collect duration. E.g., allow an event to start on September 15, and end on September 16.','','7.12'),('9466','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Collect an end date','','7.12'),('9467','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Select the timezone handling method for this date field.','','7.12'),('9468','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Repeating date','','7.12'),('9469','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora/field-settings?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora&destinations[1]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Repeating dates use an ''Unlimited'' number of values. Instead of the ''Add more'' button, they include a form to select when and how often the date should repeat.','','7.12');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9470','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Default date','','7.12'),('9471','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','No default value','','7.12'),('9472','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Describe a time by reference to the current day, like ''+90 days'' (90 days from the day the field is created) or ''+1 Saturday'' (the next Saturday). See !strtotime for more details.','','7.12'),('9473','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Relative default value','','7.12'),('9474','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Default end date','','7.12'),('9475','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Same as Default date','','7.12'),('9476','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Relative default value for end date','','7.12'),('9477','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','pm','ampm','7.12'),('9478','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Date entry options','','7.12'),('9479','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Control the order and format of the options users see.','','7.12'),('9480','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Time increments','','7.12');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9481','','default','1 minute','','7.12'),('9482','','default','5 minute','','7.12'),('9483','','default','10 minute','','7.12'),('9484','','default','15 minute','','7.12'),('9485','','default','30 minute','','7.12'),('9486','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','The location of date part labels, like ''Year'', ''Month'', or ''Day'' . ''Above'' displays the label as titles above each date part. ''None'' doesn''t label any of the date parts. Theme functions like ''date_part_label_year'' and ''date_part_label_month'' control label text.','','7.10'),('9487','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Display all day checkbox','','7.10'),('9488','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Determines whether to display the ''All Day'' checkbox to the user.','','7.10'),('9489','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','More settings and values','','7.12'),('9490','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Date entry','','7.12'),('9491','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Starting and ending year','','7.12'),('9492','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Starting year','','7.12'),('9493','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Enter a relative value (-9, +9) or an absolute year such as 2015.','','7.12'),('9494','/dday/admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields/field_hora?destinations[0]=admin/structure/types/manage/session/fields','default','Ending year','','7.12');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9495','sites/all/modules/date/date_api/date_year_range.js','default','@count year from now','','none'),('9496','sites/all/modules/date/date_api/date_year_range.js','default','@count years from now','','none'),('9497','/dday/node/add','default','Una sesión, taller, bof o sprint que se llevará a cabo durante el Drupal Day.','','7.12'),('9498','/dday/node/add/session','default','Empty ''End date'' values will use the ''Start date'' values.','','7.10'),('9499','/dday/node/add/session','default','@field_name Start date','','7.10'),('9500','/dday/node/add/session','default','@field_name End date','','7.10'),('9501','/dday/node/add/session','default','Date','datetime','7.10'),('9502','/dday/node/add/session','default','E.g., @date','','7.10'),('9503','/dday/node/add/session','default','Time','datetime','7.10'),('9504','/dday/node/add/session','default','Hora','','7.12'),('9505','/dday/node/add/session','default','Hora Start date','','7.10'),('9506','/dday/node/add/session','default','Hora End date','','7.10'),('9507','/dday/node/6','default','!start-date to !end-date','','7.12'),('9508','/dday/node/6','default','@label -  start date (!name)','','7.12'),('9509','/dday/node/6','default','@label -  start date','','7.12'),('9510','/dday/node/6','default','@label - end date (!name:!column)','','7.12'),('9511','/dday/node/6','default','@label - end date:!column','','7.12'),('9512','/dday/admin/structure/views/view/calendar/edit','default','Position: @position, format: @format.','','7.10'),('9513','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','The contextual filter values is provided by the URL.','','7.10'),('9514','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Date format options','','7.10'),('9515','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','The date format used in titles and summary links for this argument. The default format is based on the granularity of the filter, i.e. month: @example_month, day: @example_day.','','7.10');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9516','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Custom summary date format','','7.10'),('9517','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','A custom format for the title and summary date format. Define a php date format string like ''m-d-Y H:i'' (see <a href="@link">http://php.net/date</a> for more details).','','7.10'),('9518','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Set the allowable minimum and maximum year range for this argument, either a -X:+X offset from the current year, like ''-3:+3'' or an absolute minimum and maximum year, like ''2005:2010'' . When the argument is set to a date outside the range, the page will be returned as ''Page not found (404)'' .','','7.10'),('9519','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Dates to compare','','7.10'),('9520','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Start/End date range','','7.10'),('9521','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Only this field','','7.10'),('9522','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','If selected the view will check if any value starting with the ''Start'' date and ending with the ''End'' date matches the view criteria. Otherwise the view will be limited to the specifically selected fields. Comparing to the whole Start/End range is the recommended setting when using this filter in a Calendar. When using the Start/End option, it is not necessary to add both the Start and End fields to the filter, either one will do.','','7.10'),('9523','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Add multiple value identifier','','7.10'),('9524','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Add an identifier to the view to show which multiple value date fields meet the filter criteria. Note: This option may introduce duplicate values into the view. Required when using multiple value fields in a Calendar or any time you want the node view of multiple value dates to display only the values that match the view filters.','','7.10');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9525','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Select one or more date fields to filter with this argument.','','7.10'),('9526','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/config-item/calendar/page_3/argument/date_argument','default','Method of handling multiple date fields in the same query. Return items that have any matching date field (date = field_1 OR field_2), or only those with matches in all selected date fields (date = field_1 AND field_2). ','','7.10'),('9527','/dday/admin/structure/views/view/calendar/preview/page_3/ajax','default','Empty day','','7.12'),('9528','/dday/admin/structure/views/view/calendar/preview/page_3/ajax','default','Prev','date_nav','7.10'),('9529','/dday/admin/structure/views/view/calendar/preview/page_3/ajax','default','Next','date_nav','7.10'),('9530','/dday/admin/structure/views/view/calendar/edit/page_3','default','Tipo de sesión','','7.12'),('9531','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/pager_options','default','This pager works together with a Date or Content date field contextual filter. If a Date filter has been added to the view, this pager will provide back/next paging to match the granularity of that filter (i.e. paging by year, month, week, or day). The filter must also be configured to use a DATE default value. If there is no Date contextual filter on this view, or if it has not been set to use a default date, the pager will not appear.','','7.10'),('9532','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/pager_options','default','Date identifier','','7.10'),('9533','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/pager_options','default','The query identifier to use when fetching date data from in the URL. Note that if you have more than one display in the same view that uses the date pager (like a page and a block), the pager id must be different for each one or both will change when the pager value changes.','','7.10'),('9534','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/pager_options','default','Pager position','','7.10');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9535','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/pager_options','default','Where to place the date pager, on the top, bottom, or both top and bottom of the content.','','7.10'),('9536','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/pager_options','default','Link format','','7.10'),('9537','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/pager_options','default','The format for pager link urls. With the Pager format, the links look like ''calendar/?date=2020-05''. The Clean format links look like ''calendar/2020-05''. The Clean format links look nicer but the Pager format links are likely to work better if the calendar is used in blocks or panels.','','7.10'),('9538','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','The calendar row plugin will format view results as calendar items. Make sure this display has a ''Calendar'' format and uses a ''Date'' contextual filter, or this plugin will not work correctly.','','7.10'),('9539','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Add new date link','','7.10'),('9540','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Display a link to add a new date of the specified content type. Displayed only to users with appropriate permissions.','','7.10'),('9541','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Legend Colors','','7.10'),('9542','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Set a hex color value (like #ffffff) to use in the calendar legend for each content type. Items with empty values will have no stripe in the calendar and will not be added to the legend.','','7.10'),('9543','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Stripes','','7.10'),('9544','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Add stripes to calendar items.','','7.10'),('9545','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Based on Content Type','','7.10');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9546','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Based on Taxonomy','','7.10'),('9547','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Based on Organic Group','','7.10'),('9548','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Term field','','7.10'),('9549','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Select the taxonomy term field to use when setting stripe colors. This works best for vocabularies with only a limited number of possible terms.','','7.10'),('9550','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','You must add a term field to this view to use taxonomy stripe values. This works best for vocabularies with only a limited number of possible terms.','','7.10'),('9551','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/row_options','default','Vocabulary Legend Types','','7.10'),('9552','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/style_options','default','Calendar type','','7.10'),('9553','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/style_options','default','Display as mini calendar','','7.10'),('9554','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/style_options','default','Display the mini style calendar, with no item details. Suitable for a calendar displayed in a block.','','7.10'),('9555','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/style_options','default','Calendar day of week names','','7.10'),('9556','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/style_options','default','Display overlapping items, with scrolling','','7.10'),('9557','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/style_options','default','Display overlapping items, no scrolling','','7.10'),('9558','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/style_options','default','Select whether calendar items are displayed as overlapping items. Use scrolling to shrink the window and focus on the selected items, or omit scrolling to display the whole day. This only works if hour or half hour time grouping is chosen!','','7.10');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9559','/dday/admin/structure/views/ajax/display/calendar/page_3/style_options','default','Optionally group items into columns by a field value, for instance select the content type to show items for each content type in their own column, or use a location field to organize items into columns by location. NOTE! This is incompatible with the overlapping style option.','','7.10'),('9560','/dday/admin/structure/date','default','Dates and calendars can be complicated to set up. The !date_wizard makes it easy to create a simple date content type and related calendar. ','','7.10'),('9561','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Machine-readable name. Allowed values: (a-z, 0-9, _). If this is not an existing content type, the content type will be created.','','7.10'),('9562','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Date widget type','','7.10'),('9563','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Display a matching second date field as a ''End date''.','','7.10'),('9564','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','The recommend type is Datetime, except for historical dates or dates with only year or month granularity. Older or incomplete dates should use the Date type (an ISO date).','','7.10'),('9565','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Year range','','7.10'),('9566','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Range of allowed years, oldest to newest. ''-1:+1 means oldest date is one year back, newest is one year forward from current year.','','7.10'),('9567','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Date timezone handling','','7.10'),('9568','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Timezone handling should be set to ''none'' for granularity without time elements.','','7.10'),('9569','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Add calendar blocks to a region','','7.10'),('9570','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Fill out the following form to auto-create a date content type, with a datetime field and matching pre-configured calendar. A calendar and upcoming events block will be created, an ical feed will be added to the calendar, and the mini calendar, calendar legend, and upcoming events blocks will be added to the sidebar of the default theme. Nodes created from this new content type will include a link to the calendar, and the calendar will have a link to the ''add new date'' form. You can also add new date fields to an existing content type by entering the existing content type name instead of creating a new one.','','7.10');
INSERT INTO `locales_source` VALUES ('9571','/dday/admin/structure/date/date_wizard','default','Only a limited set of options are displayed here to make this easy to set up. Once the date has been created you will be able to make other changes to the date settings and add other fields to your new content type on the Manage fields screen, and make changes to the calendar on the Views edit page.','','7.10'),('9572','/index.php','default','Module !module cannot be enabled because it depends on the following modules which could not be found: !unmet_dependencies','','7.10'),('9573','/index.php','default','!module requires !unmet-projects','','7.10'),('9574','/index.php','default','The following projects have unmet dependencies:\n!list\nWould you like to download them?','','7.10'),('9575','/index.php','default','Nodes represent the main site content items.','','7.12'),('9576','','default','Uploaded file.','','7.12'),('9577','/index.php','default','Remark or note that refers to a node.','','7.12'),('9578','/index.php','default','Taxonomy terms are used for classifying content.','','7.12'),('9579','/index.php','default','Taxonomy vocabularies','','7.12'),('9580','/index.php','default','Vocabularies contain related taxonomy terms, which are used for classifying content.','','7.12'),('9581','/index.php','default','Enables modules to work with any entity type and to provide entities.','','7.12'),('9582','/index.php','default','Provides a field that can reference other entities.','','7.12'),('9583','/index.php','default','Provides token replacements for all properties that have no tokens and are known to the entity API.','','7.12'),('9584','','default','false','','7.12'),('9585','','default','true','','7.12'),('9586','','default','None.','','7.12'),('9587','','default','Import failed.','','none'),('9588','','default','Unpublished','','none'),('9589','','default','clone','','7.12'),('9590','','default','export','','7.12'),('9591','','default','Overwrite','','7.12'),('9592','','default','The number of votes that have been cast on a poll node.','','none'),('9593','','default','The length of time the poll node is set to run.','','none');
